--- stdout
--- stderr
Detect the content type of files with Google's Magika model

Usage: magika [OPTIONS] <PATH>...
       magika --list-content-types [--json]

Arguments:
  [PATH]...  Files or directories to identify. `-` reads standard input

Options:
  -r, --recursive               Identify the files inside directories instead of the directories themselves
      --no-dereference          Identify symbolic links as such instead of following them
  -m, --prediction-mode <MODE>  How confident the model must be for its prediction to be used [default: high-confidence] [possible values: high-confidence, medium-confidence, best-guess]
  -l, --label                   Print the label (e.g. `rust`) instead of the description
  -i, --mime-type               Print the MIME type (e.g. `application/x-rust`) instead of the description
  -s, --output-score            Append the score of the prediction
      --json                    Print a JSON array with the prediction and content type of each path
  -j, --jobs <N>                Identify this many files at a time. Defaults to the number of processors
      --list-content-types      List all content types and exit. Combine with --json for JSON
  -h, --help                    Print help (see more with '--help')
  -V, --version                 Print version
